d 'EPLOT': module to draw forest plots and coefficient plots from data, stored estimates, matrices or frames
d
d  eplot draws forest plots and coefficient plots through one
d interface from four sources: estimates and confidence limits held
d as variables in memory (for example meta-analysis results), the
d active or stored estimation results, a matrix, or a graph-ready
d frame. The input mode is detected from the arguments. Several
d stored models can be overlaid for comparison. Options select,
d drop, rename, group and sort coefficients, exponentiate them,
d draw a log scale, add capped confidence intervals, weighted
d markers, diamonds for pooled estimates, prediction intervals,
d significance stars and colors, a column of formatted estimates
d with confidence intervals, heterogeneity statistics, reference
d lines and favors labels, and apply journal style presets. The
d plotted estimates and limits, their p-values when available, the
d number of display rows and the twoway command that was executed
d are returned in r(). 
d
d KW: forest plot
d KW: coefficient plot
d KW: meta-analysis
d KW: effect estimates
d KW: confidence intervals
d KW: regression results
d KW: model comparison
d KW: graphics
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261030
d
d Author: Timothy P Copeland, Karolinska Institutet
d Support: email timothy.copeland@@ki.se
d
f eplot.ado
f eplot.sthlp
